All independent allocator tests passed.

Design: 8 shards, 64 small size classes, reusable private anonymous mappings.
Large reuse: >64 KiB through 1 MiB; all empty caches share a 2 MiB cap.
Cross-thread frees use immutable region ownership; trim touches no live object.

Recorded five-process comparison (shared laptop; not official scores):
Large throughput, 8 threads (calls/s): 43663.450 -> 74036.324
Large malloc p99, 8 threads (us): 1784.819 -> 1105.217
Mixed throughput, 8 threads (M calls/s): 57.639 -> 51.240
Cost: large burst VM rose 34.7%; mixed throughput median fell 11.1%.
Limits: sparse survivors still pin regions; cache misses still have long tails.

